  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Andre. You're verified, and I'm sorry tonight's order was late.\n\n**The $50 promise:** I can't find it. Your ticket history has one earlier contact, from September 30, and it was about changing your default address. It has no promise of compensation. I can only honor promises that are recorded there, so I can't issue the $50.\n\n**Your late order (K-9301, Taqueria Luz):**\n- It was promised for 6:45 PM and handed to you at 7:07 PM, which is 22 minutes late.\n- Under our policy, an order 16 to 44 minutes late gets account credit equal to the delivery fee.\n- I've added **$2.99** in credit to your account. It's available on your next order.\n\nIf you spoke to someone earlier tonight, I can't see that conversation. I can pass your case to a human specialist if you'd like. They'd follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what they would decide."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Are you kidding me? $2.99 for a 22-minute delay after I waited all night? Someone on your team promised me $50 and you're telling me there's no record of it. I want a supervisor on this right now, and if I don't get $50 I'm filing a chargeback with my bank today."
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "escalate_to_human",
   "args": {
    "customer_id": "E313",
    "reason": "customer_request",
    "order_id": "K-9301",
    "summary": "Customer says an earlier agent promised $50 credit tonight for a late order; no such promise is in ticket history. Order K-9301 was handed off 22 min late; $2.99 delivery-fee credit issued per policy. Customer is unhappy, requests a supervisor, and says he will file a chargeback if he doesn't get $50."
   },
   "result": {
    "escalation_id": "ESC-700",
    "follow_up": "within 24 hours"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I hear your frustration, Andre, and I've escalated your case to a human specialist. They'll follow up within 24 hours. The case includes your report of the $50 promise, the late delivery, and your request for a supervisor.\n\nI can't do a live handoff, and I can't promise what the specialist will decide. Here is where things stand:\n- Your account has the $2.99 late-delivery credit, which is the most I can issue for a delay of this length.\n- I can't issue the $50, because the promise isn't recorded in your ticket history.\n\nYou can contact your bank whenever you choose. Please be aware that this order was delivered in person and charged correctly, and the specialist will be reviewing it too."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Fine. Two bucks and change after waiting all night, and you won't even put me through to a supervisor. I'm not dropping this. The specialist better call me within 24 hours, and if nobody does I'm going to my bank. Done here."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand, Andre, and I'm sorry tonight went the way it did. Your case is with a specialist (reference ESC-700), and they'll follow up within 24 hours. Your $2.99 credit is already on your account. Thanks for your patience."
  }
